          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            with a notion of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mi dim
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = dim(X) \in \mathbb{N}
            and a notion of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+differential+form"}> Kähler
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms"} differential forms
            on it, the
            %em canonical bundle
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+sheaf"} canonical sheaf
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+bundle"} line bundle
            (or its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
            = succeed "-forms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "-fold" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dim
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dim(X)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exterior+product"} exterior product
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi can
                  %mo ≔
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi X
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  L_{can} \coloneqq \Omega^n_X
          %p
            of the bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1_X
            of 1-forms.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Chern+class"} first Chern class
            of this bundle is also called the
            %strong
              canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+class"} characteristic class
            or just the
            %strong canonical class
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            The inverse of the canonical line bundle (i.e. that with minus its
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Chern+class"} first Chern class
            = succeed "." do
              %em anticanonical line bundle
          %p
            Over an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+variety"} algebraic variety
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/divisor+%28algebraic+geometry%29"} divisor
            corresponding to the canonical line bundle is called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+divisor"} canonical divisor
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/square+root"} square root
            of the canonical class, hence another characteristic class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Θ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Theta
            such that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cup+product"} cup product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %mi Θ
                  %mo =
                  %mi Θ
                  %mo ∪
                  %mi Θ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 \Theta = \Theta \cup \Theta
            equals the canonical class is called a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theta+characteristic"} Theta characteristic
            (see also
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metalinear+structure"} metalinear structure
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#InComplexAnalysis In complex analytic geometry
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
            regarded over the complex numbers, then
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+differential+forms"} Kähler differential forms
            are
            %em holomorphic
            forms. Hence the canonical bundle for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi dim
                    %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dim_{\mathbb{C}}(X) = n
            is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^{n,0}
            (see also at
            = succeed ")," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dolbeault+complex"} Dolbeault complex
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+line+bundle"} complex line bundle
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surface"} Riemann surface
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genus+of+a+surface"} genus
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/degree+of+a+coherent+sheaf"} degree
            of the canonical bundle is
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mi g
                    %mo −
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 g - 2
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theta+characteristic"} Theta characteristic
          %p
            In particular the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Chern+class"} first Chern class
            of the canonical bundle on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sphere"} 2-sphere
            is
            %em twice
            that of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basic+line+bundle+on+the+2-sphere"} basic line bundle on the 2-sphere
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^2(S^2, \mathbb{Z}) \simeq \mathbb{Z}
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization+of+the+2-sphere"} geometric quantization of the 2-sphere
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/density+bundle"} density bundle
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume+form"} volume form
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kodaira+vanishing+theorem"} Kodaira vanishing theorem
          %div
            %p
              The following table lists classes of examples of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/square+roots"} square roots
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+bundles"} line bundles
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th line bundle
                  %th square root
                  %th choice corresponds to
              %tbody
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+bundle"} canonical bundle
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theta+characteristic"} Theta characteristic
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    over
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surface"} Riemann surface
                    and
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermitian+manifold"} Hermitian manifold
                    (e.g.
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+manifold"}> Kähler manifold
                    ):
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structure"} spin structure
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/density+bundle"} density bundle
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/half-density+bundle"} half-density bundle
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+bundle"} canonical bundle
                    of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+submanifold"} Lagrangian submanifold
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metalinear+structure"} metalinear structure
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metaplectic+correction"} metaplectic correction
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/determinant+line+bundle"} determinant line bundle
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pfaffian+line+bundle"} Pfaffian line bundle
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    quadratic
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/secondary+intersection+pairing"} secondary intersection pairing
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
                    of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+theory"} self-dual higher gauge theory
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+Wu+structure"} integral Wu structure
          %h2#references References
          %p
            In the context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
